bench/fixtures/zh-en/computer.ogg
    Test-split files 2650, 953, 363, 20 and 92 (the "correct" Mandarin-English
    code-switched recordings) of CSZS, the zero resource code-switched speech
    benchmark, joined with one second of silence between them and re-encoded
    as Opus; truth.json holds their transcriptions converted to Traditional
    Chinese with OpenCC s2tw. CSZS is licensed under the MIT License and is
    described in: Kuan-Po Huang, Chih-Kai Yang, Yu-Kuan Fu, Ewan Dunbar and
    Hung-Yi Lee, "Zero Resource Code-Switched Speech Benchmark Using Speech
    Utterance Pairs for Multiple Spoken Languages", ICASSP 2024.
    Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/ky552/cszs_zh_en
